From: Tilo <tilo@tilo.so>
Subject: virtio-gpu: do not fence a CPU dumb blob flush

A guest blob that the CPU filled has no GL submit. Queuing a fenced
RESOURCE_FLUSH leaves the control-queue slot occupied until a fence
that never completes. The next present then blocks for 1-2 s and an
animation paints no frames.

Skip that fence for a dumb primary. An imported primary blob still
allocates one.
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c
@@ -366,7 +366,11 @@
 
 	drm_gem_plane_helper_prepare_fb(plane, new_state);
 
-	if (!bo || (plane->type == DRM_PLANE_TYPE_PRIMARY && !bo->guest_blob))
+	/* A CPU dumb blob has no GL submit, so a fenced flush never
+	 * completes in virgl and the control queue stalls the next present.
+	 */
+	if (!bo || (plane->type == DRM_PLANE_TYPE_PRIMARY &&
+		    (!bo->guest_blob || bo->dumb)))
 		return 0;
 
 	obj = new_state->fb->obj[0];
